    {
      "line": 3,
      "tag": "invariants/clean repair",
      "text": "masks==anchors==n_frames, no orphan events, no overlap, no empty track; script_bits = before + sum(deltas)",
      "verdict": "holds"
    },
    {
      "line": 3,
      "tag": "two cost models in one script",
      "text": "on 3 worlds the repair prices its new events with b_objid=3 while every other event in the same script uses b_objid=2. The advertised '+2 bits per swap' becomes +4, and the script_bits that `choose_operator` compares between operators is no longer a single code length.",
      "verdict": "REFUTES"
    },
    {
      "line": 3,
      "tag": "'+2 bits per swap' is one-cell only",
      "text": "delta is [2, -2, -6] for 1/2/3-cell movers; for k>=2 the repair is a net *saving*, which also means the matcher would never have picked the wrong reading there in the first place.",
      "verdict": "note"
    },
    {
